WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.630
Joe: The ‘Triad of impairments’ was
a breakthrough in its time as it

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:07.880
gave clarity to what had seemed to be
unrelated clinical phenomena and made

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.459
way for recognition of the different
levels of impairment, especially

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.430
‘high functioning’ forms of Autism.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.860
The observation about the lack of
pretend play, a seemingly small

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.600
thing, had big consequences and
would have a lasting impact on

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.790
diagnostic and assessment methods.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:28.610
Beth: However, for some, the ‘triad’
wasn’t perfect as it didn’t go far enough.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.829
It didn’t cover sensory impairment, and
the problems individuals with Autism

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:35.059
have with light, sound and touch.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.940
Previously, impairments needed to be
evident in the ‘triad’ in order for

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.860
a diagnosis of Autism to be made.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.760
Joe: But as we have said before
there are always new ideas coming

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.140
forward and recently the well-known
‘triad of impairments’ is becoming

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.220
referred to as a ‘dyad of impairment’.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.230
The ‘Dyad of impairment’ looks
to highlight all the specific

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:59.040
difficulties people with Autism
have, combining ‘social interaction’

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.460
and ‘communication and language’,
into ‘social communication’ skills.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:07.410
Beth: And a key thing is where the
‘triad’ didn’t refer to the ‘sensory

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:11.749
needs’ of individuals with Autism, this
is now to be included in the ‘restricted

00:01:11.779 --> 00:01:13.640
and repetitive behaviour’ sections.

